       Primitives may be combined using:

              A parenthesized group of primitives and operators.

              Negation (`!!' or `nnoott').

              Concatenation (`&&&&' or `aanndd').

              Alternation (`||||' or `oorr').

       Negation  has  the  highest  precedence.  Alternation and concatenation
       have equal precedence and associate left to right.

       If an identifier is given without a keyword, the most recent keyword is
       assumed.  For example,
            nnoott hhoosstt vs aanndd ace
       is short for
            nnoott hhoosstt vs aanndd hhoosstt ace
       which should not be confused with
            nnoott ((hhoosstt vs oorr ace))

